          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Anxiety sits in the mental and behavioural chapter. Where would a physical symptom of it, like palpitations, be classified?",
          "answer": "Palpitations, as a physical symptom, are classified under Chapter 18 of the ICD-10, which is dedicated to symptoms, signs, and abnormal findings (codes R00 to R99). Specifically, palpitations fall into the codes starting with R00, which covers symptoms related to the circulatory system. This includes various issues like abnormal cardiac findings and elevated blood pressure in individuals without a diagnosis (source: ICD-10-CM Chapter 18).\n\nWhile anxiety, which you mentioned, is categorized under Chapter 5, relating to mental and behavioral disorders (codes F01 to F99), its physical symptoms, like palpitations, are recorded in Chapter 18. This classification shows how symptoms can be documented separately from the underlying mental health conditions they may be associated with.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
